  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday) \nIssued at 1041 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nAs we reach Thursday, there are still some inconsistencies between \nmodels. However, it does seem as though stronger ridging may end up \nwinning out over the mid-state and the latest NBM is definitely \npicking up on this. What was upper 80s to about 90 for the second \nhalf of the week has now become mid 90s for areas west of the \nCumberland Plateau right into next weekend. NBM MaxT probs each \nafternoon starting Thursday through next weekend of seeing 95+ \ndegrees stands at 70-80% for many west of the Plateau. Only 48 hours \nago, it was only 30-40%. Big change. Dew points will be the big \nchallenge, but even at these environmental temps, we may only be in \nadvisory territory. Again, I don't think we rule out a stray storm\nfor the second half of the week, but if temps are going to get \nthis warm because of a strengthening ridge, convection should be \nat a minimum each afternoon.",
